     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>I started working with CTMM a few weeks ago, and after a few days and stumbling around got it to work successfully. Using data I uploaded to movebank, I fly through the code without erros. </div><div><br></div><div>I am now returning to old code to rerun it and produce figures, but when I go to run my old code</div><div><br></div><div>PM20tel&lt;-as.telemetry(PM20, timeformat=&quot;&quot;,timezone=&quot;UTC&quot;,projection=NULL,timeout=Inf,na.rm=&quot;row&quot;,</div><div>                      mark.rm=FALSE,drop=TRUE)</div><div><br></div><div>I get this error</div><div><br></div><div>&quot;Error in proj[1, 2] : subscript out of bounds&quot;</div><div><br></div><div>Google tells me that this means I am trying to access an array out of its boundary, but none of the fixes I have found seem to be appropriate for the dataset,</div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:15px\"><br></span></div><div>Any advice or help anyone can give would be hugely appreciated,</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers</div><div><br></div><div>Josh</div><div>-- <br><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">PhD Student</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Queen&#39;s University Belfast</span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);